# fantasyfootball weekly automation.
# Install with: sudo crontab crontab.example
# (edit the `cd` path first to match where the repo actually lives on
# this machine, then re-save before installing.)
#
# Mirrors the production Windows Task Scheduler cadence: Tuesday 07:00,
# Thursday 07:00, Sunday 08:00, US Central time. The run time IS load-bearing: the
# CLI resolves the current NFL week from the schedule, so the run time
# directly determines which week gets operated on and logged. Running too
# early (e.g. on a UTC host, if these times were misread as UTC) means
# Sleeper's week hasn't rolled over yet and Monday Night Football's stats
# haven't landed -- the script would silently overwrite the git-tracked
# prediction log with a stale/wrong snapshot.
#
# CRON_TZ pins these times to US Central regardless of the host's system
# timezone. This requires a cron implementation that supports per-line/file
# CRON_TZ (Vixie-cron/cronie); most modern Linux cron daemons do.
CRON_TZ=America/Chicago
#
# Cron runs jobs with a minimal PATH (typically /usr/bin:/bin), which can
# miss `docker` on systems where it's installed elsewhere (e.g.
# /usr/local/bin, or /snap/bin for snap-installed Docker on Ubuntu).
PATH=/usr/local/bin:/usr/bin:/bin:/snap/bin
#
# Day-of-week: 0=Sunday, 2=Tuesday, 4=Thursday.
0 7 * * 2 cd /path/to/fantasyfootball && docker compose exec -T app ./weekly-refresh.sh tuesday >> data/outputs/logs/cron.log 2>&1
0 7 * * 4 cd /path/to/fantasyfootball && docker compose exec -T app ./weekly-refresh.sh thursday >> data/outputs/logs/cron.log 2>&1
0 8 * * 0 cd /path/to/fantasyfootball && docker compose exec -T app ./weekly-refresh.sh sunday >> data/outputs/logs/cron.log 2>&1
